{"from": "site:salamis-cyprus", "type": "attests", "to": "place:salamis-cyprus", "grade": "A", "note": "The excavated city of Salamis (Cyprus Exploration Fund from the late 19th century; 1952-1974 campaigns) - the place is a documented, excavated site."}
{"from": "site:paphos-nea-paphos", "type": "attests", "to": "place:paphos", "grade": "A", "note": "Excavated Nea Paphos, the Roman provincial capital with Roman villas, agora, Asklepion, theatre and the Tombs of the Kings - the place named in 13:6-13."}
{"from": "site:antioch-pisidia", "type": "attests", "to": "place:antioch-pisidia", "grade": "A", "note": "The excavated Roman colony Colonia Caesarea at Yalvac (Michigan 1924; Ramsay; Taslialan): Augusteum, Propylon, Tiberia Platea, western gate - the city of 13:14-50."}
{"from": "site:perga", "type": "attests", "to": "place:perga", "grade": "A", "note": "Excavations at Perge from 1946 uncovered a theatre, stadium, palaestra, temple of Artemis and two churches - the city of 13:13-14."}
{"from": "site:seleucia-pieria", "type": "attests", "to": "place:seleucia-pieria", "grade": "A", "note": "Seleucia in Pieria, the Hellenistic seaport of Antioch ad Orontes, survives in ruins with inner and outer Roman harbours - the port of 13:4."}
{"from": "artifact:sergius-paulus-boundary-stone", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-07-sergius-paulus-proconsul", "grade": "D", "note": "Disputed identification: the stone names a L. Sergius Paulus, ex-consul, appointed curator alvei Tiberis in AD 47 - it does not name Cyprus. Mitford: identification with the proconsul of Cyprus is 'at best a conjecture, now somewhat weakened by Myres' reading of IGR iii, 935'."}
{"from": "artifact:sergius-paulus-boundary-stone", "type": "attests", "to": "person:sergius-paulus", "grade": "D", "note": "Names a L. Sergius Paulus (curator of the Tiber banks, AD 47); the identification with the Cyprus proconsul of Acts 13:7 is a conjecture (Mitford), not established."}
{"from": "artifact:soli-proconsul-paulus-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-07-sergius-paulus-proconsul", "grade": "D", "note": "Disputed: the Soli (Cyprus) inscription mentions a proconsul Paulus, but Hogarth dated it to the mid-1st century and Mitford argued on epigraphic grounds that it 'cannot be dated earlier than this and is probably considerably later', so it cannot be pinned to the Claudian proconsul of Acts 13."}
{"from": "text:cassius-dio-54-4-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-07-cyprus-proconsular-province", "grade": "B", "note": "Dio 54.4.1: Augustus in 22 BCE 'restored to the people both Cyprus and Gallia Narbonensis... and thus proconsuls began to be sent to those provinces also' - Cyprus as a public (senatorial) province under a proconsul, the office-title of 13:7."}
{"from": "artifact:miletus-godfearers-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-16-god-fearers", "grade": "C", "note": "A Miletus theatre seat inscription (CIJ 748) reserves a place 'of the Jews who are also (called) God-fearers' (theosebeis): Gentile sympathizers attached to a Jewish community in Roman Asia Minor. Later than Acts 13 and from a different province - context, not the Antioch congregation."}
{"from": "artifact:theodotos-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-15-reading-law-prophets", "grade": "C", "note": "The Theodotos inscription (Jerusalem, 1st century BCE-70 CE) records a synagogue built for 'the reading of the Law' and the teaching of the commandments - synagogue Torah reading as an institution in the period; Jerusalem, not Pisidia, and it does not record the Prophets reading or the invitation."}
{"from": "artifact:great-isaiah-scroll", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-34-isaiah-55-3-quoted", "grade": "B", "note": "The pre-Christian Great Isaiah Scroll (c. 125 BCE) contains the entire Book of Isaiah, including the quoted Isaiah 55:3 - the calibration's B case for a quoted passage; it attests the pre-Christian form of the quotation, not the speech."}
{"from": "artifact:great-isaiah-scroll", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-47-isaiah-49-6-quoted", "grade": "B", "note": "The pre-Christian Great Isaiah Scroll (c. 125 BCE) contains the entire Book of Isaiah, including the quoted Isaiah 49:6 - the calibration's B case; it attests the pre-Christian form of the quotation, not the mission application."}
{"from": "text:tacitus-annals-15-44", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-13-28-pilate-death", "grade": "B", "note": "Tacitus, Annals 15.44: Christus 'suffered the extreme penalty... at the hands of one of our procurators, Pontius Pilatus' - confirms the execution under Pilate that 13:28 presupposes; the 'found no cause for death' detail is beyond it."}
