{"from": "claim:ac-13-28-pilate-death", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-02-11-pilate-governor", "note": "Same event told differently: Acts 13:28 adds that the Jerusalem rulers found no cause for death yet asked Pilate to have him killed; Matthew 27:2, 11 records the delivery to and judgment by the governor Pilate."}
{"from": "claim:ac-13-15-reading-law-prophets", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-04-16-sabbath-synagogue-custom", "note": "Same Sabbath-synagogue custom in the diaspora (Antioch of Pisidia) and in Nazareth: standing readings of the Law and Prophets; Acts 13:15 adds the rulers' invitation to a visiting speaker."}
{"from": "claim:ac-13-15-reading-law-prophets", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-13-14-archisynagogos", "note": "Both passages presuppose the archisynagogos (ruler of the synagogue) officiating; Acts 13:15 has the rulers (plural) send the invitation."}
{"from": "claim:ac-13-51-shook-dust", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-14-shake-dust", "note": "The same gesture Jesus instructed for rejecting towns in Matthew 10:14 is carried out by Paul and Barnabas leaving Pisidian Antioch (Acts 13:51)."}
{"from": "claim:ac-13-43-proselytes", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-13-16-god-fearers", "note": "Two distinct sympathizer groups in one synagogue audience: proselytes (13:43) had become converts, while 'you who fear God' (13:16, 26) names uncircumcised God-fearers."}
{"from": "claim:ac-13-35-psalm-16-10-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-02-25-31-psalm-16-quoted", "note": "The same Psalm 16 'decay' argument made twice in Acts: by Peter at Pentecost (2:25-31) and by Paul at Pisidian Antioch (13:35-37)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-22", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-samuel-13-14", "note": "Acts 13:22 quotes/combines 1 Samuel 13:14 ('a man after my heart') in the speech's retelling. Cross-reference, not evidence (docs/calibration.md)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-33", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:psalm-2-7", "note": "Acts 13:33 quotes Psalm 2:7 ('You are my Son. Today I have become your father.'). Cross-reference, not evidence (docs/calibration.md)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-34", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:isaiah-55-3", "note": "Acts 13:34 quotes Isaiah 55:3 ('the holy and sure blessings of David'). Cross-reference, not evidence; the Great Isaiah Scroll carries the passage (B)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-35", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:psalm-16-8-11", "note": "Acts 13:35 quotes Psalm 16:10 ('You will not allow your Holy One to see decay'). Cross-reference, not evidence (docs/calibration.md)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-41", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:habakkuk-1-5", "note": "Acts 13:41 quotes Habakkuk 1:5 as the closing warning. Cross-reference, not evidence (docs/calibration.md)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-47", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:isaiah-49-6", "note": "Acts 13:47 quotes Isaiah 49:6 ('a light for the Gentiles'). Cross-reference, not evidence; the Great Isaiah Scroll carries the passage (B)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-28", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-23-04", "note": "Luke 23:4: Pilate finds no basis for a charge; Acts 13:28 retells it as 'they found no cause for death'."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-28", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-02", "note": "Matthew 27:2: Jesus handed over to Pilate the governor; Acts 13:28 retells the delivery to Pilate."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-29", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-59", "note": "Matthew 27:59: Joseph takes the body and lays it in his own tomb; Acts 13:29 retells 'they took him down from the tree, and laid him in a tomb'."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-51", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-14", "note": "Matthew 10:14: shake the dust off your feet against a rejecting town; Acts 13:51 shows the gesture performed."}
{"from": "passage:ac-13-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-04-16", "note": "Luke 4:16: Sabbath synagogue attendance 'as was his custom'; Acts 13:14-15 shows the same custom at Pisidian Antioch with the invitation to speak."}
